Page type: QtWidgets list + details, kept in QtWidgets (docs/page-design.md §8; a QML port is not small). Search field
stays first, the Known Types tree below, details on the right. Config, mimeapps/xml writing and save() are unchanged.
NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Changed:
- Button/placeholder labels use the "…" character: "Add…" (types, patterns, applications), "Edit…", "Apply To…", search
  placeholder "Search for file type or filename pattern…" (HIG: ellipsis on buttons that open something).
- The two QGroupBox sections ("Filename Patterns", "Application Preference Order") are flat (title without frame), as §8.
  Uncertain: how Breeze draws a flat QGroupBox.
- "Reading file types…" label under the tree, only after 150 ms.
- Relabel table inventory/relabel/kcm_filetypes.tsv (outer repo); the aliases "File Associations" etc. are already in
  ia/layout.json. 20 inventory rows kept (ksr markers); inventory_check --kcm kcm_filetypes --strict: 0 lost, full run 0 lost.

Speed (cause found in code, keditfiletype/filetypesview.cpp readFileTypes via load()): load() disabled the widget and built
the whole tree synchronously: QMimeDatabase::allMimeTypes() (about a thousand types), sort, and per type a TypesListItem
whose MimeTypeData constructor runs initFromQMimeType(): QStandardPaths::locateAll for the type's XML file, opening and
parsing it (mimetypedata.cpp:69-125). The KSycoca/KApplicationTrader lookup per type is already lazy (m_bFullInit) and was
left. Now readFileTypes() returns at once; QTimer::singleShot(0) reads allMimeTypes and readNextBatch() creates the items
in ~10 ms batches (same sorted order), with a generation counter against a second load(). The search field works while it
fills: new rows honour the current filter (group items start hidden when a filter is set and show when a child matches).
After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: QMimeType needs <QMimeType> in filetypesview.h (added); the page is enabled during the fill, so a
very early click on Add or Apply sees only the types read so far (new types are added to m_majorMap as before).

